items.prose:
A client put `capital` pounds into a fund at the end of 1992. `fund()` returns the fund's yearly returns as a pandas Series indexed by year, 1993 to 2024. The years arrive in no particular order.

`wealth_chart(rets, capital)` returns one Axes holding:

- the client's wealth in £ at the end of each year, as a line labelled `Wealth`. It starts at `capital` in the year before the first return;
- the running peak of that wealth over the same years, as a dashed line labelled `Running peak`;
- a legend naming both lines;
- a y axis on which a 30% fall has the same height in any year. Label it with its unit, £.

Leave `rets` unchanged. `short()` returns a second fund's returns, 2016 to 2021, in the same form.

